# Test: the fleet interface opens on the sample estate
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-ui-1 Wiring Test and AC-1 -- a build carrying the
#            sample tag, started web-only, opens /fleet/ on the estate
#            dashboard of the sample estate inside the shell
# PREVENTS: a sample build whose fleet route is unmounted, or whose shell
#           renders without its tree or its dashboard
#
# Goal: prove a browser reaches the fleet shell through the real web server.
# Method: open /fleet/ and read the page state: the shell's three regions by
# id, the sample marker in the header, and the Devices card of the estate
# dashboard, whose total is the sample estate's 44 devices
# (sample/estate_test.go TestSampleEstateInvariants). A unit test renders the
# handler alone (TestFleetShellRendersSampleEstate); only a browser proves the
# route is mounted in the hub and the page loads in a browser.
#
# A ze built without ze_fleet_ui_sample skips this case with the reason.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_fleet_ui_sample:state=present
option=timeout:value=60s
option=viewport:width=1600:height=1000

action=open:path=/fleet/
expect=element:id=fleet-sidebar
expect=element:id=fleet-tree
expect=element:id=fleet-content
expect=html:contains=Sample data
expect=html:id=fleet-content:contains=fleet-donut-total-figure">44<
expect=url:contains=/fleet/
